# {{name}}

Made from [hapi-factory](https://github.com/{{owner}}/hapi-factory)'s repo contract: work is planned in planning PRs, built by the factory, and merged by the maintainer.

## Quick start

You need [mise](https://mise.jdx.dev). It installs every other tool at its pinned version.

```bash
mise install && mise run setup && mise run check
```

`mise tasks` lists the rest: `fmt`, `lint`, `test`, `smoke` and `scan`.

## How changes land

Every change reaches `main` through a pull request, with the `ci / gates` check green and the maintainer's approval. Planning PRs bring work orders and their acceptance tests; the factory opens one PR per work order; only the maintainer merges. [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md) has the details, and [SECURITY.md](SECURITY.md) says how to report a vulnerability.

